    "Fuel density 0.74 kg/L for 2-stroke petrol/oil mix.",
    "Gear and inertia are Stage 3 engineering estimates, to be refined in Stage 4.",
    "Gear: mains 0.25 m ahead of CG, 1.5 m track; steerable tailwheel (assumed, +/-30 deg) 3.75 m behind the mains; fuselage about 11 deg nose-up on the ground (wing about 12.5 deg with its 1.6 deg incidence; tall ultralight main gear).",
    "Struts sized for ~4 cm static compression on the mains and ~0.5 critical damping.",
    "Inertia from Roskam radii of gyration for light singles (Rx 0.248, Ry 0.338, Rz 0.393) with an assumed 5.4 m length.",
    "Stage 4 flight model (estimates tuned to the CLAUDE.md targets; see docs/STATUS.md):",
    "Derivatives are typical light-aircraft values scaled for a tail arm of ~3.4 m and a 1.8 m2 tailplane; static margin ~12% chord.",
    "Hirth F-33 full-throttle curve shaped from the 20.6 kW at 6500 rpm rating; single cylinder two-stroke; 2.5:1 belt at 95%.",
    "Aero: CLalpha ~4.7/rad, zero-lift alpha -4.6 deg (cambered ultralight section), CLmax 1.82 at 18 deg; CD0 0.085 (open frame, exposed pilot, struts and wires); induced drag k = 1/(pi e AR) with whole-aircraft e 0.9, AR 5.96. Beyond the stall CL/CD blend into flat-plate values.",
    "Propeller 60x28 in fixed-pitch wood: CT/CP curves shaped for P/D 0.47, peak efficiency ~0.75 near J 0.4-0.5; loading set so static rpm is ~5300 and full-power level rpm ~6700 (typical F-33 installation).",
    "Wing rigging incidence 1.6 deg (user check 2026-10-19): fuselage attitude reads 0 deg in level flight at 75% throttle (~47 kt), about +10 deg in the full-power climb at Vy and about -10 deg in a 45 kt idle descent.",
